CalcUI
======

CalcUI is a retained-mode GUI toolkit for Odin, built on SDL3 and the Runa
text shaping engine.

Third-party components
----------------------

Runa — src/GUI/dependencies/Runa
    Copyright (c) the Runa authors.
    Licensed under the zlib licence.
    See src/GUI/dependencies/Runa/LICENSE for the full text.

    Runa is used as a git submodule. It supplies the font parsing, the
    shaping (GSUB/GPOS), the bidirectional text handling, the line
    breaking and the rasterization that the text pipeline of CalcUI is
    built on. CalcUI does not modify Runa; the submodule is used as it
    is published.

SDL3 — the window and the two rendering backends
    Copyright (c) the SDL authors.
    Licensed under the zlib licence.
    SDL3 is used through the Odin vendor collection (vendor:sdl3), so
    it is not part of this repository.

Skald — parts of the widget behaviour and of the PNG decoder
    Copyright (c) the Skald authors.
    Licensed under the BSD 2-Clause licence.

    Ported code carries the notice required by clause 2 of that
    licence, which says that the copyright notice, the conditions and
    the disclaimer have to be kept, and that the software has to be
    marked as changed. Every file that holds ported code says so at
    its top:

        //* Ported from Skald (BSD-2-Clause) and altered for CalcUI.

    Only the behaviour was ported. The implementation was written
    against CalcUI's own model: a retained widget tree with real
    widget identity, instead of Skald's immediate-mode scratch record.

